.git
# The workflow file is re-included below: test_toolchain_declared.py compares
# the ast-grep pin in it against the Dockerfile's, and a check that cannot run
# in the container is a check that silently does not run there.
.github/**
!.github/workflows/tests.yml
.pytest_cache
**/__pycache__
**/*.pyc
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
dotfiles
experiments
references
decisions
node_modules

# specs/ is excluded, EXCEPT the contract schemas. The image's first self-test
# run failed on test_contract_file_is_valid_json_schema, which reads the
# authoritative contract — a test that passed on every dev laptop and could
# never pass in the container. Making it skip when specs/ is absent was the
# wrong fix: a drift check that silently does not run reports clean, which is
# the whole defect class this repo is about. The contracts are ~5KB; ship them
# so the check runs in every environment.
specs/**
!specs/003-gate-portfolio/contracts/**
